            <ArticleTitle>Effects of statins on C-reactive protein and interleukin-6 (the Ludwigshafen Risk and Cardiovascular Health study).</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>305-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>This report provides preliminary evidence that statins may lower C-reactive protein levels by interfering with the generation and/or release of C-reactive protein in the liver rather than by modulating inflammatory processes in the vessel wall.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
